From: NeoDarwin
Subject: [PATCH] iokit: build IOPCIFamily and NeoDarwin's PCI host bridge

P1-09 checkpoint 2 enumerates PCIe with Apple's open IOPCIFamily
(IOPCIFamily-726.0.5, the macOS 26.0 release, APSL; overlaid at
iokit/ndpci/IOPCIFamily) on the ACPI host bridges that NeoDarwin's ACPI
platform publishes (patch 0018). IOPCIFamily is a kext, and its platform
half is not open: Intel Macs had AppleACPIPCI and Apple silicon Macs have
their SoC's PCIe driver. NeoDarwin's (kernel/neodarwin/pci, overlaid at
iokit/ndpci) is an IOPCIHostBridge over ECAM. Like the rest of the
platform they are compiled into the kernel, since kcgen links no kexts
until M5 (docs/kernel/pci.md).

This patch lists for arm64 the seven IOPCIFamily sources that build there
(IOPCIBridge, IOPCIConfigurator, IOPCIDevice, IOPCIDeviceMappedIO,
IOPCIMessagedInterruptController, IOPCIRange, IOPCITraceEventBuffer;
AppleVTD, IOPCIDeviceI386 and IOPCIBridgeLegacy are Intel-only) and
NeoDarwin's three (the ECAM registry, the host bridge, and a driver for
QEMU's edu test device that proves INTx delivery), with their search
paths: IOPCIFamily's own headers, the compat TargetConditionals.h of
patch 0010, and compat os/availability.h and IOKit/dart/IODARTKeys.h.
The ACPI platform's objects see nd_pci.h too: it registers MCFG's ECAM
windows and routes INTx through _PRT. The built-in personalities match
the host bridge to PNP0A08/PNP0A03 nubs, IOPCIFamily's IOPCI2PCIBridge to
PCI-to-PCI bridges (the kext's Info.plist personality, IOPCIClassMatch
0x0604), and the edu driver to 1234:11e8.

Rebase-risk: low (appended entries; applies after 0018).
---
--- a/iokit/conf/files.arm64
+++ b/iokit/conf/files.arm64
@@ -180,5 +180,21 @@
 iokit/ndacpi/acpica/source/components/utilities/utxfinit.c	standard
 iokit/ndacpi/acpica/source/components/utilities/utxfmutex.c	standard
 
+# NeoDarwin PCI (kernel/neodarwin/pci, overlaid at iokit/ndpci): the ECAM
+# host bridge and configuration access, and Apple's IOPCIFamily-726.0.5
+# (@apple_iopcifamily, APSL, at iokit/ndpci/IOPCIFamily): the sources of its
+# kext that compile for arm64; AppleVTD, IOPCIDeviceI386 and
+# IOPCIBridgeLegacy are Intel-only
+iokit/ndpci/nd_pci_ecam.c	standard
+iokit/ndpci/NeoDarwinPCIHostBridge.cpp	optional iokitcpp
+iokit/ndpci/NeoDarwinPCIEduTest.cpp	optional iokitcpp
+iokit/ndpci/IOPCIFamily/IOPCIBridge.cpp	optional iokitcpp
+iokit/ndpci/IOPCIFamily/IOPCIConfigurator.cpp	optional iokitcpp
+iokit/ndpci/IOPCIFamily/IOPCIDevice.cpp	optional iokitcpp
+iokit/ndpci/IOPCIFamily/IOPCIDeviceMappedIO.cpp	optional iokitcpp
+iokit/ndpci/IOPCIFamily/IOPCIMessagedInterruptController.cpp	optional iokitcpp
+iokit/ndpci/IOPCIFamily/IOPCIRange.cpp	optional iokitcpp
+iokit/ndpci/IOPCIFamily/IOPCITraceEventBuffer.cpp	optional iokitcpp
+
 # tightbeamc generated implementation files
 ./Exclaves/IOService.tightbeam.c		optional iokitcpp config_exclaves
--- a/iokit/conf/Makefile.template
+++ b/iokit/conf/Makefile.template
@@ -71,6 +71,24 @@
 $(foreach o,$(ND_ACPICA_OBJS),$(eval $(o)_CFLAGS_ADD += -DND_ACPICA_CORE -include $(ND_ACPI)/acnd.h -I$(ND_ACPICA)/include -w))
 $(foreach o,nd_acpi_osl.o NeoDarwinACPIPlatform.cpo IOACPIPlatformDevice.cpo,$(eval $(o)_CFLAGS_ADD += \
 	-I$(ND_ACPI) -I$(ND_ACPI)/include -I$(ND_ACPICA)/include))
+
+# NeoDarwin's PCI (patch 0022). IOPCIFamily is kext code: it finds its own
+# headers (IOKit/pci, PCIDriverKit) at its root, the compat TargetConditionals.h
+# (libpthread's, patch 0010), and NeoDarwin's compat os/availability.h and
+# IOKit/dart/IODARTKeys.h, which the kext gets from the SDK and the closed
+# DART driver. -w: upstream warnings are not NeoDarwin's to fix here.
+# NeoDarwin's PCI files and the ACPI platform, which routes INTx and passes
+# AML's configuration accesses to ECAM, see nd_pci.h and the IOPCIFamily and
+# IOKit/acpi headers; IOPCIFamily's classes are marked deprecated for kexts.
+ND_PCI = $(SRCROOT)/iokit/ndpci
+ND_IOPCI = $(ND_PCI)/IOPCIFamily
+ND_IOPCI_OBJS = IOPCIBridge.cpo IOPCIConfigurator.cpo IOPCIDevice.cpo IOPCIDeviceMappedIO.cpo \
+	IOPCIMessagedInterruptController.cpo IOPCIRange.cpo IOPCITraceEventBuffer.cpo
+$(foreach o,$(ND_IOPCI_OBJS),$(eval $(o)_CFLAGS_ADD += -I$(ND_IOPCI) -I$(ND_PCI)/compat \
+	-I$(SRCROOT)/libkern/ndpthread/compat -w))
+$(foreach o,NeoDarwinPCIHostBridge.cpo NeoDarwinPCIEduTest.cpo nd_pci_ecam.o nd_acpi_osl.o NeoDarwinACPIPlatform.cpo \
+	IOACPIPlatformDevice.cpo,$(eval $(o)_CFLAGS_ADD += -I$(ND_PCI) -I$(ND_IOPCI) -I$(ND_PCI)/compat \
+	-I$(SRCROOT)/libkern/ndpthread/compat -I$(ND_ACPI)/include -Wno-deprecated-declarations))
 
 #
 # Diagnostic opt-outs.  We need to make this list empty.
--- a/iokit/KernelConfigTables.cpp
+++ b/iokit/KernelConfigTables.cpp
@@ -46,6 +46,21 @@
     "     'IOProbeScore'    = 1000:32;"
     "   },"
     "   {"
+    "     'IOClass'         = NeoDarwinPCIHostBridge;"
+    "     'IOProviderClass' = IOACPIPlatformDevice;"
+    "     'IONameMatch'     = ('PNP0A08', 'PNP0A03');"
+    "   },"
+    "   {"
+    "     'IOClass'         = IOPCI2PCIBridge;"
+    "     'IOProviderClass' = IOPCIDevice;"
+    "     'IOPCIClassMatch' = '0x06040000&0xffff0000';"
+    "   },"
+    "   {"
+    "     'IOClass'         = NeoDarwinPCIEduTest;"
+    "     'IOProviderClass' = IOPCIDevice;"
+    "     'IOPCIMatch'      = '0x11e81234';"
+    "   },"
+    "   {"
     "     'IOClass'         = IOExclaveProxy;"
     "     'IOProviderClass' = IOService;"
     "     'IOExclaveProxy'  = 1:32;"
